# The build context is the repository, and these are the parts of it that either
# do not belong in an image or would defeat the layer cache.
#
# web/node_modules is the important one twice over: it is the largest thing in
# the tree, and the console stage installs its own from the lockfile - copying
# the host's over the top would put whatever is on this machine into the image
# instead of what the lockfile says.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Build output of a local `go build` or a gate run. The image builds its own.
/flowy
/smoke
*.test

# Nothing in here changes what is built, and .git in particular is large.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.firecode-*

# The gate's own scratch and anything a run left behind.
run-tests.log
